The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$p$$$ ($$$1 \le n \le 3000$$$, $$$10^8 \leq p \leq 10^9$$$, $$$p$$$ is prime) — the number of cities and the modulo.

It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3000$$$.', 'For each test case, output $$$n+1$$$ integers: the $$$i$$$-th integer should be the number of arrays that satisfy the conditions for $$$k = i-1$$$.', 'STANDARD', 10000, 1048576, 65536, true, NOW());
